            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>All Lovers tend to be extroverts by default. Since you are predisposed to matters such as romance and friendships, you likewise have the most optimal mindset for these things. You are <span class="text-orange">lively and joyful</span>, and you never run out of ways to keep a person engaged. You might see this quality shine particularly well on dates, where your very presence is enough to make a good impression on your prospective partner.</p>
              <p>Aside from extroversion, you also think of the larger group and the common good. This is even more evident when you are involved in a romantic arrangement, because you often allow the other person’s side to be fully heard. You listen to people and are empathetic on that account. For all those reasons, therefore, the people around you are willing to give you the same treatment.</p>
              <p>Add to that, intuition is yet another strong point of the lover. As a general rule, this means that you tend to obey your impulses and <span class="text-orange">go with your emotions a lot</span>. This means that you tend to make decisions which are illogical. Regardless, all of these decisions are likely going to be guided by good motives-- and the people around you know this. To this end, they are going to be kind to you and give you everything you need to fulfill your wishes.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Another aspect of the Lover is turbulence. There are times when you are simply passionate about the things that you do, and there are even more times when you can be whimsical. This bodes well for a relationship, but poorly for a crisis, because you will often fall prey to your anxieties and worst opinions about yourself.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
