  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Lover, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As the master of love and relationships, you are certainly the fun-loving type. You know that love is like an endless tug of war, where the perpetual tension of pushing and pulling is what makes a relationship fun and exciting.</p>
              <p>Given such, you’re the type to constantly make games and <span class="text-orange">explore new things</span> within the relationship. You never settle for just one thing, even when you love settling for just one person. Instead of simply comforting you and your partner with what’s familiar, you always give extra effort to seek out new ways to do the same old things in a relationship. </p>
              <p>This characteristic often makes the relationship blossom. As you and your partner explore new things, constant growth is present both as a couple and an individual. Because you seek to constantly spark that candle, love will always be in the air even when it is not valentine’s day. </p>
              <p>However, try to be wary about this tendency of your archetype. Being fun-loving is not always a positive trait, especially when you’re slowly seeking out things outside of the relationship. If you equate love and meaning with <span class="text-orange">happiness and excitement alone</span>, then it won’t be long before you’ll see someone else in your life. </p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Instead, try to realize that suffering and pain is also part of what makes a relationship beautiful. Think of the challenges and struggles that you were able to bear with your partner. Think of those magnanimous moments where both of you have conquered the impossible. Surely, not all of them will be “fun” but they are definitely meaningful. </p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Moreover, openness is one of the key tendencies of a Lover in love. Since they are the type who accepts life as it unfolds, they never limit themselves to what tradition or society sets. That’s why the Lover archetype is one of the few who can truly understand the meaning of love – boundlessness. </p>
          <p>Whereas other archetypes can be limited by norms or structures in society, the Lover sees no bounds. Instead, they follow their heart. They follow their passion and pursue it no matter what it takes. They see life beyond what’s set in stone and <span class="text-orange">accept the differences among individuals</span>. </p>
          <p>As such, you are the type who’s practically open to everyone. While you aspire for beauty and knowledge, you have the tendency to see beyond it. You know, after all, that beauty is in the eye of the beholder. How you see is what makes you happy, and this openness allows you to appreciate the many nuances of being in a relationship. </p>
          <p>Given this strength, the kind of relationships that you’ll build with others is also <span class="text-orange">open and boundless</span>. While you invest in someone, you’ll constantly explore new things with them as you allow life to unfold. </p>
          <p>While you know how to enjoy those Netflix over pizza at home nights, you’re never really limited to it. Seeking a new hobby? Eager to travel to other countries? Looking for ways to do charity? Your openness will not only unlock the right person but also the doors to meaning and freedom as you and your partner get to explore the beauty of life itself. </p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Lover is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
