  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Lover</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Lover is a combination of extroversion, intuitiveness, we-centeredness, and turbulence. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to health services, sales and marketing, and middle management. With their passionate and committed nature, a Lover can blossom in these paths. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/health-service-lover.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Health Services</h5>
              <p>Health services is one of the key areas where you can become effective. As an archetype, you are passionate and dedicated to whatever you choose to do. These strengths affect how you perceive life and how you think it should go along.</p>
              <p>As such, having a career in the health services is a good way for you to live your life. With your unparalleled passion, the Lover in you can empower you to take on the challenges of pursuing the arduous road of medicine. Whether you become a nurse, doctor, or even pharmacist, the level of dedication that’s needed in these professions is close to none.</p>
              <p>More importantly, pursuing a career in the health services requires having both ideals and the heart of service. While other archetypes may lack these, you as a Lover feels intuitively connected to such. As you pursue your career in this sector, you’ll feel the imminent desire to attain the best results possible.</p>
              <p>Add to that, you are also known to be resilient. You simply won’t give up. You will stop at nothing in achieving what you want. As such, this will push you forward, even when the road is bleak and winding. After all, a career in the field of medicine will have endless twist and turns.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Even then, your resilience will prove as useful. And in doing so, you also get to inspire others towards your mission. Through your concrete actions in this field, people will be moved by your actualized ideals and the outright positive energy that you exude.</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/sales-marketing-lover.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Sales and Marketing</h5>
              <p>A career on sales and marketing is certainly something that suits the Lover. Since the Lover archetype is naturally gifted at alluring others, closing a sale is definitely something that comes naturally from them.</p>
              <p>In selling something, people often go for the same products. Just look at the market , even our cellphones don’t have much of a difference from each other. But when a skilled salesperson appears, some wire in our head is suddenly activated, as if to pull us closer to the sale.</p>
              <p>As such, the Lover is excellent in doing those. Since they are naturally gifted to allure others, the Lover understands what it takes to close a sale. From the way they smell, to the actuations that they make, the Lover is excellent at portraying everything that the prospect wants to see. Gaining the trust of the prospect in an instant, the Lover can easily charm their way through to close that deal.</p>
              <p>Add to that, the Lover also knows how to translate this into business strategy. When tasked to create advertisements and promotional activities, the Lover is great at conceptualizing what works since they can apply the same interpersonal skills.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Given such, sales and marketing certainly fits you. You may not see it at first, especially when you’re not driven by money. Even then, try to look at how you convince others to believe you. That alone is a good indicator that you’ll probably do well in this field!</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/middle-management-lover.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Middle Management</h5>
              <p>Often, one of the problems with middle management is the promotion of Silo mentality. As various teams and its members decide to withhold information to other teams, such crippling logic often prevents the company to achieve its best interests.</p>
              <p>Similarly, such toxic traits are present among middle managers who see themselves as bosses instead of leaders. Constantly abusing their power, these middle managers satiate themselves by letting out their stress on those below their ranks.</p>
              <p>Yet, apart from these two toxic traits, a Lover archetype excels at becoming that motivational leader. As a manager, you will be loved by your team and even those from other departments.</p>
              <p>Because of your ability to understand how people think, managing them to become efficient team members is something that comes naturally from you. Knowing the value and importance of group effort, you know how to motivate your team to do what’s expected of them.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>More importantly, your interpersonal skills also help you prevent internal strife. As your intuition grants you the power to see through things, you can prevent conflict even before it happens. Such acumen is highly valued for it ensures that everything remains balanced within the workplace.</p>
          <p>And as you do these things, people will simply love you for it. They will feel recognized instead of simply being cogs in a machine. In turn, your passion and dedication actualizes into something that brings appreciation back to you.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
